            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Influence on Modern Neuroscience</strong><br>\nCajal's findings on the nervous system influenced the course of modern neuroscience. He is often referred to as the father of modern neuroscience for his contributions to understanding the individual cellular structures of the brain and nervous system.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Cajal's Later Work</strong><br>\nLater in his life, Cajal continued to write and explore neuroscience. He published several influential books and articles, theorizing about the direction of future research and the potential for regeneration of nerve cells, which sparked ongoing study.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy of Santiago Ramón y Cajal</strong><br>\nSantiago Ramón y Cajal passed away in 1934, but his legacy endures. His work is still referenced in neuroscience research and education, and his theories continue to inspire scientists. Cajal’s blend of artistic talent and scientific insight remains a model for multidisciplinary exploration.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
